# 1. Executive Summary

BrightCare Medical Group relies on multiple third-party vendors, cloud providers, contractors, and service providers to support healthcare operations, business functions, technology infrastructure, and patient care services.

This Third-Party Vendor Risk Analysis was conducted to:

- Identify risks associated with third-party vendors
- Evaluate vendor security controls
- Assess operational and compliance risks
- Reduce exposure to cybersecurity threats
- Improve protection of Protected Health Information (PHI)

The assessment identified several high-risk areas related to vendor access, cloud services, remote support, and handling of sensitive information.

---

# 2. Purpose

The purpose of this assessment is to:

- Evaluate vendor cybersecurity risks
- Assess vendor access to organizational systems and PHI
- Identify weaknesses in third-party security controls
- Support HIPAA compliance requirements
- Improve vendor governance and oversight
- Reduce operational and cybersecurity risks

---

# 3. Assessment Scope

This assessment included vendors involved in:

- Cloud hosting
- Managed IT services
- Healthcare applications
- Email services
- Backup services
- VoIP systems
- Security services
- Billing and payment systems
- Remote support services
- Data processing services

---

# 4. Assessment Methodology

The assessment methodology included:

- Vendor inventory review
- Security questionnaire analysis
- Contract and agreement review
- Access review
- Data handling review
- Compliance evaluation
- Risk scoring
- Security control analysis

The assessment aligned with:

- HIPAA Security Rule
- NIST Cybersecurity Framework
- Vendor risk management best practices

